cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite Foundation Branch Paper 002 for the current Foundation account and the
  specific immutable branch-paper DOI for any other results used. Later
  branches remain under full V1/V2-to-V3 reconciliation.
title: "Ernos Labs Smithian Fold Theory Open Science Platform and Knowledge Tree"
type: software
version: 3.0.0-foundation-successor
date-released: 2026-07-24
authors:
  - family-names: Smith
    given-names: Maria
    email: Maria.Smith.Sftoe@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/MettaMazza/ernos-labs-sft-platform"
url: "https://github.com/MettaMazza/ernos-labs-sft-platform"
abstract: >-
  Accessible Python clean-room reconstruction of Smithian Fold Theory with one
  fail-closed admission engine, exact candidate enumeration, unique-survivor
  forcing, adverse controls, independent reconstruction, sealed empirical
  comparison and immutable receipts. Published v1 branch papers remain citable
  at their individual DOIs, but current-completeness status is withdrawn while
  all 356 V1 and 407 V2 registered results receive categorical ownership and
  same-strength V3 disposition. The current Foundation successor reviews all
  763 entries, closes 32 of 32 Foundation-owned obligations and documents 16
  admitted theorems across 5,222 generated candidate classes.
keywords:
  - Smithian Fold Theory
  - exact arithmetic
  - computational proof
  - empirical validation
  - clean-room reconstruction
  - open science
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
